Note: with a constant hazard, the per-step posterior CP probability p(r_t=0) is identically H by construction (both posterior branches scale with the same predictive mass), so the data-driven statistic is the run-length distribution: E[r] above; downward resets of E[r] in the curves mark detected changepoints.
